The code was edited to reflect correct syntax and not the csharp code. The assert statements for the given examples were inserted. Please note that the exact syntax may vary based on the function or program using this assertion. The "OLD" keyword is used in this format to signify the original state of a variable, and "RET" is used to refer to the return value of a function.--------------------
Debug.Assert(Count == OLD(Count) - 1 || Count == OLD(Count));
</code> 
That's because every time an element is removed from the list, the Count property should be equal to the previous count - 1 or remain the same. The Assert.Contains() method can check whether a given value is present in the list. However, since the requirement starts with "array list size decreases by one or remains the same after remove" and does not mention the specific value to be checked or position of the element to be removed, we don't know which of these conditions should return false. So, for now, I made an assertion on the Count property after removal of elements. If the condition changes in future then please re-run test and modify the assertion accordingly.--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(_size) - Count != 1 || OLD(_size) == Count);
</code>
